        "mapping": "The pump’s pressure plays the role of voltage, the litres per second play the role of current, and the narrowness of the pipe plays the role of resistance."
      },
      "key_rule": {
        "statement": "The voltage across a resistor equals its resistance multiplied by the current flowing through it, so for a fixed resistance the current doubles when the voltage doubles.",
        "formula": "\\q{U} = \\q{R} \\times \\a{I}"
      },
